te_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107967#pullrequestreview-3012251146","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107967","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107967#pullrequestreview-3012251146"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107967"}},"submitted_at":"2025-07-11T23:21:39Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3012257702,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6zi2em","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally on Windows 11 24H2 (rebased on top of `master` https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/c6d130abd9188f313e6701d01a0ddd6ea32166a0), it mostly works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [physics_interpolation_gyro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21191387/physics_interpolation_gyro.zip) (same as https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1223, but with gyro support added)\r\n*Hold <kbd>L2</kbd> to freeze gyro so you can readjust your aim.*\r\n\r\nTested controllers so far:\r\n\r\n- DualSense (wired)\r\n- DualSense Edge (wired)\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Touchpad button, touchpad finger coordinates, LED control, battery status, accelerometer and gyroscope all work.\r\n\r\n- I couldn't get adaptive triggers to work, even when double-checking the source code to make sure I'm passing valid values. I've tried to call the method in `_ready()` (after waiting 1 frame) and `_process()` to no avail. No errors/warnings appear in the console.\r\n\r\n- Enabling gyroscope, accelerometer and setting a light color only works if you wait 1 frame in `_ready()` using `await get_tree().process_frame`. Otherwise, the method calls seem to be ignored.\r\n\r\n- There's no `Input.get_joy_light()` counterpart to `Input.set_joy_light()`. Does SDL provide an API for this? If implemented, it should retrieve the actual gamepad color that may have been set by another application. Otherwise, I would leave things as-is.\r\n\r\n- `Input.set_joy_light()` should call `Color.srgb_to_linear()` on the color passed as parameter (the testing project does this in the script). This will make the color's brightness/saturation better match what you see on screen. Currently, `Color(0.2, 1, 0.2)` looks quite pastel on a DualSense Edge, while it should be a mostly saturated green.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107967#pullrequestreview-3012257702","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107967","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107967#pullrequestreview-3012257702"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107967"}},"submitted_at":"2025-07-11T23:27:15Z","commit_id":null}]